# disc_ribs.cam — bosses on a ROUND blank, two of them ON its edge (Phase
# 47 slice 1; DECISIONS.md → "DRAFT: Phase 47 opens…", fork 2A, and "Phase
# 47 slice 1…"). The shape of the first real part's upper half, self-authored
# so it ships: a `Face` level whose loop is the part's SILHOUETTE, drawn two
# chord tolerances past the round and chorded at the one tolerance exactly
# as the recognizer writes it (`geometry.part`); two rim pads whose outer
# arc is the round to three decimals; two L-shaped bosses facing each other
# across a slot 1.1 tool diameters wide — one millimetre of room for a
# tool standing beside either wall.
#
# What this pins. The containment lint is QUIET: a vertex drawn on the round
# to three decimals is on it (the region's `ON_THE_BLANK`, not a 1e-6 guard
# — the pads' corners land up to 0.0005 past the exact circle, as the real
# part's ribs do), and a `Face` past the blank in plan is the pocket's case,
# air the region clips. So the entry restriction READS every op instead of
# declining on a feature the lint doubted, and `--rest-report` claims.
#
# The L-bosses are slice 2's subject: the wall facing the slot is the FIRST
# edge of the loop each `Side` drives, so its lead reads the slot. (The
# engine arm normalises a CW boss to CCW, so the loop it drives starts at
# the authored LAST vertex and runs the list backwards: the slot wall is
# listed last, and traversed up for LW, down for LE.) Slice 1's lead — one
# diameter off the path along the ray from the loop's vertex-average
# centroid — pointed past the bar's end into air; since slice 2 it is the
# path's void-side normal at its first vertex, as far as the stock model
# says there is room: 1.000mm, which the program says (`tests/lead_tests.rs`).
# Rim pads: the same normal, a whole diameter of air, nothing said.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Cylinder(dia=120, h=30, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

# The level: `Level` in geometry.part (the silhouette, 173 points).

# Rim pads, CW: the outer arc at r 60, every 5°, the inner at r 48.
feature RimN ProfileBoss(extent=10.0
    -20.521 56.382
    -15.529 57.956
    -10.419 59.088
    -5.229 59.772
    0.000 60.000
    5.229 59.772
    10.419 59.088
    15.529 57.956
    20.521 56.382
    16.417 45.105
    12.423 46.364
    8.335 47.271
    4.183 47.817
    0.000 48.000
    -4.183 47.817
    -8.335 47.271
    -12.423 46.364
    -16.417 45.105
)
feature RimS ProfileBoss(extent=10.0
    20.521 -56.382
    15.529 -57.956
    10.419 -59.088
    5.229 -59.772
    0.000 -60.000
    -5.229 -59.772
    -10.419 -59.088
    -15.529 -57.956
    -20.521 -56.382
    -16.417 -45.105
    -12.423 -46.364
    -8.335 -47.271
    -4.183 -47.817
    0.000 -48.000
    4.183 -47.817
    8.335 -47.271
    12.423 -46.364
    16.417 -45.105
)

# The L-bosses, CW, the slot-facing wall first.
feature LW ProfileBoss(extent=10.0
    -38.000 -20.000
    -38.000 -8.000
    -20.500 -8.000
    -20.500 20.000
    -5.500 20.000
    -5.500 -20.000
)
feature LE ProfileBoss(extent=10.0
    20.500 20.000
    20.500 -8.000
    38.000 -8.000
    38.000 -20.000
    5.500 -20.000
    5.500 20.000
)

run End(tool=T5, surface=Level, stepover=4.0)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=RimN)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=RimS)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=LW)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=LE)
